A UNIQUE index added over rows that repeat: not a rebuild, so SQLite says
no as the index is made, not as rows are copied. Nothing changes.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'soup'), (2, 'soup');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX dish_name ON dish (name);

